    "body": "## Motivation\n\nUntracked KDA prefill forwards `(output, h)` from FlashKDA or CuTe DSL to callers expecting a tensor, causing failures such as `AttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'shape'` in gated normalization.\n\nRelated: #39925, #39926, #40124. The existing FlashKDA PRs fix the producer return contract; this alternative normalizes both supported return forms at the shared caller and also covers CuTe DSL.\n\n## Modifications\n\nUnpack tuple results immediately after dispatcher.extend(), regardless of state tracking. For a bare tensor, set h=None. Continue consuming h only on the existing tracking path.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Isolated execution of the actual forward_extend caller tail: five cases covering bare output, tuples with None or intermediate states, and tracking on/off. Confirmed the original untracked tuple leak, corrected tensor output, and unchanged forwarding of intermediate states to tracking.\n- Repository pre-commit checks and `git diff --check` passed. The branch-name guard was excluded.\n- No PyTorch, Triton, or GPU is available in this checkout, so full kernel/model tests were not run here. Isolated checks are not committed CI tests.\n- Reporter-provided combined validation with this and the separate safe-gate dispatch fix (#41121): Kimi-K3 with FlashKDA prefill and FlashInfer decode, 356-token health-check prefill HTTP 200, 120-token generation completed, zero tracebacks. This is functional validation, not an accuracy benchmark.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run. No kernel math changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format and lint checks passed.\n- [ ] Add registered CI regression tests.\n- [x] No new user-facing options or documentation changes required.\n- [ ] Full model accuracy and speed benchmarks.\n- [x] Follow existing code style.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35995154475](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35995154475)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35995154270](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35995154270)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35995154498](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35995154498)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
